Backport of the Qt 6.9 qyieldcpu.h fix, gating the <arm_acle.h> include on
__ARM_ACLE.  Two problems it solves:

  * macOS/aarch64: Apple Clang sees __has_builtin(__yield) as true, but calling
    __yield() without <arm_acle.h> is a -Werror implicit-declaration.
  * x86, any libclang parser (e.g. shiboken building PySide6): clang's
    multi-target resource dir ships arm_acle.h even on x86, and that header
    #errors ("ACLE intrinsics support not enabled") off-ARM.  A BARE
    `#if __has_include(<arm_acle.h>)` therefore breaks x86 clang parses; gating
    on __ARM_ACLE includes it only where it is valid.

Originally fixed the qt6 macos/arm64 build failure:

    src/corelib/thread/qyieldcpu.h:35:5: error: implicitly declaring
      library function '__yield' with type 'void ()'
      [-Werror,-Wimplicit-function-declaration]
    note: include the header <arm_acle.h> or explicitly provide a
      declaration for '__yield'

--- a/src/corelib/thread/qyieldcpu.h
+++ b/src/corelib/thread/qyieldcpu.h
@@ -9,6 +9,14 @@
 #include <QtCore/qprocessordetection.h>
 #include <QtCore/qtconfigmacros.h>
 
+// ARM ACLE header declares __yield() — needed on Apple/aarch64 Clang where
+// calling __yield() without it is a -Werror implicit-declaration. Gate on
+// __ARM_ACLE (not a bare __has_include): clang ships arm_acle.h on x86 too,
+// where it #errors off-ARM and breaks libclang parsers like shiboken (Qt 6.9).
+#if defined(__ARM_ACLE) && __has_include(<arm_acle.h>)
+#  include <arm_acle.h>
+#endif
+
 #ifdef Q_CC_MSVC_ONLY
 // MSVC defines _YIELD_PROCESSOR() in <xatomic.h>, but as that is a private
 // header, we include the public ones
